   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 534 of the laws of 1993, amending the education law\nrelating to physical therapy assistants, in relation to the effectiveness\nthereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S10066",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10066-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 534 of 1993",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10066\n\nSPONSOR: STAVISKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 534 of the laws of 1993, amending the education\nlaw relating to physical therapy assistants, in relation to the effec-\ntiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the current statutory authorization relating to physical ther-\napist assistants in home care settings by continuing the law through\nJune 30, 2030.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill amends section 2 of chapter 534 of the laws of\n1993, as amended by chapter 281 of the laws of 2022, to extend the expi-\nration date of the law from June 30, 2026, to June 30, 2030.\n\nSection two provides that the act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrent law allowing certain provisions relating to physical therapist\nassistants is scheduled to expire on June 30, 2026. This bill would\nextend those provisions for four additional years, through June 30,\n2030, so that the existing framework may remain in effect without inter-\nruption. Continuing the law helps preserve stability for providers and\npatients while allowing the State to maintain the current approach\nalready authorized in statute. This is an extender bill and does not\nappear to make new substantive policy changes beyond extending the\nsunset date.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter 534 of the laws of 1993. Amended by chapter 281 of the laws of\n2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
